      "message": "fix(2d): turn a contour seam lead only when it crosses its own ring\n\nOn a round-cornered outside plate, the ring's seam falls on a fitted\ncorner arc. A linear lead along that arc's end tangent crossed the ring\nnext to the seam, and verify held the post on each level, with tabs or\nwithout.\n\nA new seam_tangents (lead_seam.rs) checks the full lead at a closed\nring's seam against the ring's own feeds, by the verifier's crossing\nlaw. Only a crossing lead is mirrored across the other end's tangent,\nand only if the mirror does not cross. Every other ring keeps its\ntangents, so the #3053 regression (#3111: a moved seam and a reversed\nvertical entry arc on a plain rectangle) does not come back.\n\nFixes #3019\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
